// Calibration: Review Stale Data
// Purpose: Soft flag when the record is not valid for the current calendar year
// Category: Data Quality → Confidence Gate (Soft Flag)
//
// WHAT IS CURRENCY (in this library and the ExtMCP processor)?
// Year validity, not linear decay:
//   1.0  record year >= the current calendar year (or, for a decay-fed caller, fresh)
//   0.0  missing year, unparsable year, or a superseded fee-schedule year
//
// A linear-decay formula (1 - age/365) flagged current CY2026 fee schedules in
// November. Annual schedules are valid until superseded; they do not decay.
// Use a decay scorer only for data that really ages continuously, and keep this
// threshold if you feed that scorer: currency < 0.6.
//
// With the processor's 0/1 currency, currency < 0.6 matches a superseded year.
// That is REVIEW, matching flag_stale_result.cel. It is not a hard block.
//
// VERDICT: FLAG for review; the result is still returned.

currency < 0.6
